# OT-side servers — on the 192.168.100.0/24 OT subnet behind pp-ot-router.
# Domain-joined; auth/DNS goes to pp-dc03 (local OT DC) with pp-dc01 fallback.
#
# pp-dcs-ctrl (OT control station) FORWARDS Windows event logs but runs NO
# Sysmon, and both halves are asserted -- section 13 and section 12
# respectively. The line is INSTRUMENT vs OBSERVE: Sysmon instruments the OS
# with a kernel driver and process-level hooks, which does not belong on
# process-critical OT equipment; a universal forwarder only reads event logs
# Windows is already writing, which is ordinary practice on an HMI or
# engineering station even where an EDR agent would never be allowed.
#
# Until 2026-08-24 it produced NO telemetry at all -- no event logs, no Sysmon,
# nothing -- while it sat in [ae], a host attacks are actively run against. A
# target with zero evidence is not blind-spot realism, it is an exercise that
# cannot be scored. It reached that state structurally rather than by decision:
# this group was not a child of [splunk-forwarder], so nobody ever chose to
# exclude it. It is a child now.
[ot_servers]
pp-dcs-ctrl

